Explain why when x = 5, the expression x^2 - 10x + 17 has its minimum value.', '(x - 5)^2 >= 0, so the expression is smallest when (x - 5)^2 = 0, i.e. when x = 5.', 'x^2 - 10x + 17 = (x - 5)^2 - 8.
(x - 5)^2 is never negative and is zero when x = 5.
So the minimum value occurs at x = 5.', 'Medium', '{"tags":"sass-2022-p1,q22aii","subtopic":"Completing the square","question_type":"open","diagram_required":false}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-03T15:48:09.686Z'::timestamptz, '2026-09-03T15:48:09.686Z'::timestamptz) ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
